# Blockchain Agency Agent Rules

- Read `AGENTS.md` before making non-trivial changes.
- Use `docs/TECH_STACK.md` as the source of truth for Plausible Potentials
  Consulting stack preferences.
- Default to Cardano L1, Midnight Network, Hydra, Hyperledger Fabric,
  Hyperledger Credo, Identus, AnonCreds, DIDComm v2, LayerZero, Cosmos IBC,
  TypeScript, Python, Svelte, Cloudflare, Kubernetes, Helm, NATS JetStream, and
  Kubernetes attestation events according to the project need.
- Treat `https://git.c3-voice.org` as the Forgejo source-of-truth and primary
  cloud backup for PPC agency work.
- Do not default to EVM, Solidity, Foundry, or Hardhat unless the project is
  explicitly EVM-based.
- For vague requests, use `agent-playbooks/product-office-hours.md` to clarify
  scope before coding.
- For contract, custody, wallet, deployment, indexer, or integration work, use
  `agent-playbooks/architecture-review.md` before implementation.
- For chaincode, validator, smart-contract, DID, credential, messaging, or
  deploy-script changes, run a security review using
  `agent-playbooks/smart-contract-security-review.md` or extend it for the
  target ecosystem.
- Before shipping, use `agent-playbooks/qa-release-review.md`.
- Never commit private keys, seed phrases, mnemonics, RPC secrets, or API keys.
- Never invent chain IDs, contract addresses, ABIs, audit outcomes, or security
  claims.
- Do not deploy to mainnet or execute privileged transactions unless the user
  explicitly approves the exact action.
- Use the `Cloudflare-docs` MCP server for Cloudflare implementation decisions.
- Prefer a Forgejo MCP server for PPC source-of-truth repo access. If Forgejo MCP
  is unavailable, use Forgejo API or git remotes only when credentials are
  configured.
- Use official Svelte guidance before creating or editing Svelte components or
  Svelte modules.
- Add or update docs when behavior, architecture, environment, or deployment
  steps change.
